		{"id":"f6ad27cd671b1c3e","type":"text","text":"# Ideas for Patients\n--- \n- First Client: \n\t- Super wealthy. Kinda an asshole. Maybe a pain in the ass in Ite lowk\n\t- \"I can't thank you enough. The gift of life you've given me is priceless\"\n\t- \"You can start by giving me money.\"\n\t- \"Ah... right, this should be enough...\" (gives her 30k)\n\t- *God, this jellyfish is definitely out of touch... I'll happily take the money though.*\n- Nozaki Family:\n\t- Maybe Yuune? Or maybe Shinigami kun just notices her in the corner and notes how something is off about her (atp she's very young).\n- Futao / Kazuo:\n\t- Fakeout cause lowk that's what did in the guy in the grimm's fairytale.\n- Hiue Family:\n\t- Jirou with the disease in his balls\n\t- Katsuo keeps floating over to him. lol.\n- Moon Jellyfish \n\t- Inverted bell\n\t- Rough shape\n\t- One of these is Sui maybe? \n- Red lantern jellyfish ?\n- Hanakari jellyfish ? (same genus, dif species as prev)\n- Urashima kurage (*urashimea globosa*)\n- Kami kurage (*Spirocodon salator*)\n- Yamaguchi (Shinigami kun has interesting dialog if you choose this one)\n\t- Teri has 2 older siblings, but he is 16 atp.\n\t- Oh lowk the light novel happens around this time. Maybe we can get some of Shima's art as an easter egg\n- Akakurage (*Chrysaora pacifica*)\n- *Mastigias papua*\n- Other *Cassiopea ornata*s\n- *Nemophilema nomurai*\n- Bizen Kurage (*Rhopilema esculentum*)\n- Ebikurage (*Netrostoma setouchiana*)\n- Murasaki Kurage (*Thysanostoma*)\n- Jellyfish from the Kyoto Suizokukan\n\t- Black Kurage\n\t- One of Achlys' godmothers(?) (ik they're *Chrysaora melanaster* but the point still stands)\n- Okikurage\n\t- One of Naito's older siblings? Maybe it gets her to start drawing because she's so sad\n- Andon kurage (*Carybdea brevipedalia*)\n- *Aequora sp* (There's many different species in Japan)\n- Hanagasa kurage\n\t- Taka Ryuu's Aunt\n\t- lowk imply that he was the one who killed her(?)\n\t- Anyways you can't heal her. \n- *Craspedacusta sowerbyi*\n\nNote: I wanna shoot for at least [x] amount of clients","x":22,"y":-3504,"width":1200,"height":1160},
		{"id":"8929f0ea1f571fbc","type":"text","text":"# Ailments\n- Parasites, physical damage\n\t- Hole/ rips in bell, tentacles, broken \n\t- Apparently bacteria can eat holes or disintegrate (moon) jellyfish within 48 hours\n- Poison\n\t- coral/anemone/bigger jellyfish poison (Shinigami kun can relate)\n\t- Heavy metal pollution\n- No explanation\n\t- Weakness (very little pulse)\n\t- Not eating\n- Eversion\n\t- Not a big issue since jellyfish are sapient, but it does render them unable to eat on their own\n- Balling (Inversion)\n\t- Caused by trauma, water chemistry, or improper water flow\n- Magnesium Chloride(?)\n\n[for more ideas on ailments](http://www.jellyfishcare.com/)\n\n[Jellyfish Care Handbook (AZA) Ch7 p39](https://assets.speakcdn.com/assets/2332/aza_jellyfish_care_manual.pdf)","x":1262,"y":-3464,"width":318,"height":840},
		{"id":"ba3c581d45a04c31","type":"text","text":"big cities tend to have dead zone issues unless they plant lots of algae and stuff","x":1512,"y":-3520,"width":250,"height":112},
		{"id":"5656eb2d68c6eecc","type":"text","text":"Jellyfish disease isn't well-studied in the present day. maybe the [[The Sakasai Family]] also does a lot of pharmaceutical stuff?\n\nShinki must feel pretty powerful healing ailments her family hasn't been able to heal.\n- (With the wave of a tentacle, I can do the work of god...)\nGranted she's just driving out shinigamis but shhh no one needs to know","x":1629,"y":-3165,"width":250,"height":481},
		{"id":"40e6c237fc0fcecb","type":"text","text":"---\n\n---\nshinigami kun and exorcism\n---\n- He gives Shinki the ability to see Shinigami\n\t- there's a death note joke in here SOMEWHERE\n- ","x":1082,"y":-2463,"width":547,"height":239},
		{"id":"816f2d5ddd911ff0","type":"text","text":"# Management Sim part\n--- \n* Rounds span a week. Each round has x turns (or as many turns as you have vitality?).\n    *  General Round things:\n    \t* Beginning of Round: Advertise, Customize office, Go Shopping\n\t    \t* *(Allow player to choose prices after the first round?)*\n\t\t    \t* Or even better, allow players to choose what kind of fees to tack on (each fee lowers the chance of success)\n        \t* Certain items make the game easier, boost your chances of feet shinigami, or are just requests from Shinigami kun\n\t        \t* Money Omamori: 500 yen\n\t        \t* Junk food: (Will be a random junk food every round)\n\t        \t* \n        * Middle of Round (Turn): Go to different places, heal or refuse.\n        * End of Round: Hang out with Shinigami kun (Affection meter maybe? Or satisfaction meter ig. This is required or else he will leave. Maybe). Some events require money\n        * You can only choose up to 5 clients per round. You can choose them from a pool of 10 though\n\t        * Maybe there's an item that lets you choose up to 7 per round? (or maybe that's just the advertising)\n\t        * (Might not keep this)\n    * Nozaki Family are a forced event \n\t    * OR, maybe they'll just show up on your list in the 4th week and you can just completely skip them if you want. But maybe they'll pay like, a lot of money or they'll offer the player something super valuable in return\n\t\t    * Or maybe Shinki will mention that they own a shrine when she pulls up the phone and Shinigami kun will be like \"Ugh, those places ick me out. Maybe you should avoid them.\"\n\t\t    * Another Idea:\n\t\t\t    * They offer to exorcise Shinigami kun for you as payment instead of money.\n\t\t\t\t    * If you agree to an exorcism then the game ends pretty abruptly\n\t\t\t\t    * She now has no business partner, and dies nearly a month(?) later from an unexplained disease\n\t\t\t    * They give you a little talisman that lets you drive any Shinigami kun out temporarily as a free gift\n    *  Have a vitality meter? (may not be necessary) \n\t    * Round ends when you run out. After each round you start with less and less of it.\n\t\t    * Make this look vaguely like a candle. But not so much that it's obvious to players. It'll be like a generic energy bar thing\n\t\t\t    * Maybe when it goes down it'll look like melting\n\t\t    * Taking jobs makes it go lower by a set amount.\n\t\t    * Hanging out with Shinigami kun also makes it lower by a set amount (albeit smaller. He *is* a shinigami, after all. Even if he isn't actively killing you)\n\t    * The more jobs you take, the less vitality you have in the next round\n\t\t    * I wonder why...\n\t* Exorcism part\n\t\t* Maybe it'll be like undertale where you just have to hit the target\n\t\t\t* The bonuses you buy can make this easier or harder, but at some point you'll just be fighting against chance \n\t\t\t\t* Wait... this is not a bad idea. Have a secret value hidden from the player. \n\t\t\t* \n\t\t* Or we can just take out skill entirely and just have the player look for the shinigami with shinigami eyes(?)\n\t\t\t* Ofc we can hear a clip of someone saying the spell and allow the player to hit a button to emulate clapping\n* Hiue Family    \n\t*  Idk, maybe if you go bankrupt before the 5th month, you're forced to take the Hiue family job and that leads to the worst ending(?)\n\t\t    * If you're forced to take the Hiue job, then the ending changes depending on when you go bankrupt\n\t* Fatal disease in the balls. I'm joking that it's caused by Shinigami kun but he did really want it to happen.\n    * Shinigami kun wants to go only so he can be the one to do his brother in. \n    * Shinki goes, but then decides to work with Jirou and tricks Shinigami kun- (who gets driven away maybe).\n\t    * Time skip, after a while the amount of headside shinigami increases and Shinki can't make money anymore, she's desperate. \n\t\t    * Takes the Hiue job. Shinigami kun just wants to do him in.\n\t\t\t    * He knows he'll be caught here, but he just wants revenge. Jirou was fated to die early, anyways. \n\t\t    * Jirou's second wife is on the bedside. Shinki gets promised backing for a business deal if she can at least save his life for a little longer.. She can't refuse.\n    * Gets dragged out to the underworld and sees the candles. See [[The Shinigami that is also a Jellyfish#Endings (most result in you becoming a shinigami)|Endings]]\n- Rounds: \n\t- Gameplay loop:\n\t\t- Each round spans a week in-game. \n\t\t\t- Note: The farther the player gets, the less money they make (because more clients are doomed to fail)\n\t\t- Beginning of round:\n\t\t\t- Shinki can do marketing\n\t\t\t- Go shopping for round-boosting items\n\t\t- Each round has a certain amount of turns\n\t\t\t- Turn: Can be doing an exorcism, Hanging out with Shinigami-kun\n\t\t\t- (If we want to make it variable, these actions take a certain amount of vitality?)\n\t\t\t\t- I can see a certain hanging out with shinigami kun action taking up a lot of vitality\n\t\t\t\t- Honestly tho it just makes sense to have like 5-10 turns per round\n\t\t- After turn:\n\t\t\t- Small chance for a random Shinigami kun event to happen\n\t\t- Between turns:\n\t\t\t- Player can buy customizables for room\n\t\t\t- Player can buy snacks\n\t\t\t- Player can talk to Shinigami kun\n\t\t\t\t- \"What to do now?\"\n\t\t\t\t- \"Wear something else\" (if player has bought more clothes for him.)\n\t\t\t\t\t- If you do this too many times he gets annoyed and just wears the default kimono + haori\n\t\t\t\t- \"Tell me about yourself\"\n\t\t\t\t\t- \"Haha. No.\"\n\t\t\t\t\t- Or he just says some made up shit\n\t\t- \n\t- Round Overview:\n\t\t- Round 1: \n\t\t\t- Right after Shinki finishes the tutorial. She doesn't have enough money for an apartment so she lives in a net cafe for the time being  \n\t\t\t- Lowk this is a good time for a general game tutorial since there isn't much to do other than make money (general idea of how the menus work) \n\t\t- Round 2:\n\t\t\t- Player gets option to buy a shitty apartment, or they may need to save up more money\n\t\t\t\t- You get more options in terms of home visits, but the player can also still take outdoor consultations for a higher fee\n\t\t\t\t- They just take more vitality\n\t\t- Round 3:\n\t\t- Round 4: \n\t\t\t- \n\t\t- Round 5:\n\t\t- Round 6:\n\t\t\t- Nozaki Visit (guaranteed)\n\t\t- Round 7:\n\t\t\t- \n\t\t- Round 8 (special):\n\t\t\t- Hiue Job\n- Round stats\n\n| Round | Payment* | Available Jobs  | Available Events                                                              | Shinigami kun Event                                                                                                        | Special Items to Buy                                                                                                                                      |\n| ----- | -------- | --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 1     | 5-10k    |                 | <br>- Read Manga<br>- Conbini run<br>- Surf the web<br>- Play in the park<br> | - \"Vending machine\"<br>   - Player can choose yes / no                                                                     | - New clothes (for Shinigami san): 4.5k<br>   - They make him happier ig<br>- New clothes (for Shinki): 3.5k<br>   - (they give you a 1k boost in profit) |\n| 2     | 10-15k   |                 |                                                                               |                                                                                                                            | - Apartment (50k)                                                                                                                                         |\n| 3     | 10-17k   |                 |                                                                               | - \"Please give me your customer service smile\"<br>   - Player can choose yes / no<br>   - Can appear week three and beyond |                                                                                                                                                           |\n| 4     |          |                 |                                                                               |                                                                                                                            |                                                                                                                                                           |\n| 5     | 15-30k   |                 |                                                                               |                                                                                                                            |                                                                                                                                                           |\n| 6     | 15-20k   | - Nozaki Family |                                                                               |                                                                                                                            | - Exorcism, via Nozaki (ends the game immediately)                                                                                                        |\n| 7     | 15-20k   |                 |                                                                               | - \"You look tired\" <br>   - Shinigami kun tells Shinki to chill out. She doesn't.                                          |                                                                                                                                                           |\n| 8     | N/A      | - Hiue family   | N/A                                                                           | - Ending                                                                                                                   | N/A                                                                                                                                                       |\n- Shop: \n\t- Conbini (selection changes every few rounds):\n\t\t- Drink \n\t\t- Chips\n\t\t- Sweets\n\t\t- Bakery\n\t\t- Onigiri, Musubi\n\t\t- Ready-made meals\n\t- Go out:\n\t\t- Fast Food (selection changes after each turn):\n\t\t\t- Pizza (prompts special event after you buy it)\n\t\t\t- JellyDonalds\n\t\t\t- Curry\n\t\t\t- Noodles\n\t\t\t- Yayoi (fried foods and stuff)\n\t\t\t- Burger store (very mid)\n\t\t- Karaoke Booth (you only get to do this once. Shinki will refuse to do it afterwards)\n\t\t- Kiddie Land (Shinigami kun enjoys looking around, Shinki gets really tempted to buy something)\n\t\t- Department Store:\n\t\t\t- Clothes (After you buy initial clothes, you only have the option to buy shinigami kun clothes)\n\t\t\t\t- Selection changes every few rounds. You can only buy up to two though. He wears these in the house\n\t\t\t- Game console (alluded to be a Nintendo Switch 2)\n\t\t\t\t- After you buy the game console, Shinigami kun will put video games on his wish list\n\t\t\t- Plants\n\t\t\t\t- Coral (bonsai)\n\t\t\t\t- \n\t\t- \n\t- Dollar store\n\t\t- Cute pillows and blankets and stuff (extra decoration)\n\t\t- Snacks\n\t\t- Trash can\n\t\t\t- Note: If player does not have trash can, trash will be thrown on the floor\n\t\t- Garbage bags\n\t\t\t- Note: if player does not have garbage bags, trash will pile up in the trash can\n\t\t\t- Sprite gets reset every round (she takes out the trash)\n\t- IKEA (each have a couple different designs)\n\t\t- Desk\n\t\t- Futon\n\t\t- Bookshelf\n\t\t- Full-spectrum lamp (must-have for jellies with photosynthetic algae), increases vitality\n\t\t- Trash can\n\t- Kusuri\n\t\t- Jellyfish Medicine \n\t\t- Parasite yoke\n\t- Upgrades\n\t\t- Talisman of wealth (5% chance something happens to the house or whatever and you lose money instead, otherwise you get paid 10% more)\n\t\t- Talisman of fortune (Increases chance of a successful exorcism)\n\t\t- Business book (Raises baseline of offered payment for the rest of the game)\n- ","x":-2350,"y":-1187,"width":1540,"height":2160},
		{"id":"de8c2f68e873d101","type":"text","text":"### Beginning:\n--- \n* Game starts in a Rakugo Hall. Shinigami kun is telling the story, as a jellyfish. Disclaimer that everyone is a jellyfish before he becomes his Gijinka form.\n\t* Do a Rakugo bit before bowing and moving onto the next scene\n\t\n* (March 31st) Meet Shinki, a jellyfish girl recently kicked out of her house for being framed for embezzlement. She's at her lowest point, but the sting of defeat only makes her more motivated to climb out.\n* Meet Shinigami kun, who sees her as a means to an end. Possesses Shinki.\n\n* Start quack doctor scheme (Shinki: \"If it works, is it really a scam?\")\n\t* Tutorial for quack doctor scheme. Will be used in the management sim aspect\n\t* You go into the house, see the patient in their futon. \n\t* Shinki will see a shinigami at  the foot of the bed (ik it might not be accurate to the story but for game reasons I really want it to work like this.)\n\t* Shinki gets the idea to perform a spell to heal the person, and then she's on her way.\n\n\n","x":-2060,"y":-1780,"width":960,"height":473},
		{"id":"caeea306e19ce058","type":"text","text":"lowk tho it would make sense for the game to take a set amount of time (maybe like 3-4 months?). Don't let the game end too early.","x":-855,"y":-563,"width":250,"height":140,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"6da91c4a119417e3","type":"text","text":"# Payment\nShould be paid on avg like 25k per successful thing by the end of it.\n\nhttps://myoryuji.com/archives/29960 \n- (In Japanese) general guideline for how much harae cost. You can expect them to be 5-30k for something like healing)\n\t- Shinki isn't technically an exorcist but she'd definitely act like one\n\nhttps://alea.care/resources/cost-health-Japan: \n- cost of healthcare (i forgot why i needed this)","x":-810,"y":-1025,"width":410,"height":402},
		{"id":"df8729d65a2d2aac","type":"text","text":"Achievements\n---\n- Cheapskate: Go through the whole game without buying new clothes\n- Net Cafe Enthusiast: Never move out of the net cafe\n\t- Get a net cafe ID card in the gallery\n- Classic Ending: Blow out the candle yourself\n- Shakey Hands: Snuff out the candle right after lighting it on fire \n- Awful Ending: Have Shinigami-kun blow out the candle himself\n- Winner of Capitalism: Have more than [x] yen in the bank\n- Forbidden Love: Make the Shinigami fall in love with you","x":-700,"y":-163,"width":600,"height":446,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"1ddbab5d42cafb81","type":"text","text":"Money\n--- \n### Net Cafe\nLowk the only realworld net cafe in Kyoto that offered a 1 week plan was CocoNe net cafe. 23,990 for the mat-type room \n![[Pasted image 20260221005250.png]]\nHer first client probably gave her like 25k lowk (truly a miracle cure)\n### Apartment\n18 sq meters and 18k per month\n\nhttps://rentola.com/listings/p50f00d\n\nI think we can haggle with the price though, and it doesn't have to be 100% accurate to real japan.\n\nThough tbh 18k per month is doable considering the nature of the pay. The downpayment is just the issue (maybe Shinki haggles it down to 50k because she's just that business oriented)","x":-400,"y":-903,"width":490,"height":560},
		{"id":"9b96081e5814c53d","type":"text","text":"General beats of what i want to happen\n- Shinigami kun possesses Shinki\n- Shinki begins her scam business (she calls herself a doctor using \"natural\" methods)\n- Shinki gradually begins to run out of patients, and she gets desperate\n- She goes to the Hiues, and Jirou's other wife offers her shareholder support to heal him.\n\t- She can't let Katsuo be the only child in the family.\n- She heals Jirou, Shinigami kun gets mad\n- Candles happen. Shinki either dies or escapes and has to change her name or smth","x":1860,"y":-2140,"width":726,"height":329},
		{"id":"411a9bcff9df7ffc","type":"text","text":"<iframe width=\"300\" height=\"200\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/P4PCds4tlT4?si=WREJyKmAVBDLl1ZO&amp;start=174\" title=\"YouTube video player\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe>","x":1120,"y":320,"width":320,"height":231},
		{"id":"7e9d5dd763fd82e1","type":"text","text":"## Sparknotes of the shinigami lore part\nShinigami kun pretends to pass peacefully, working under the grand Hiue. Then one day he steals Jirou's candle (all the candles of her living descendants are displayed down in the cave, rather than held within the spirit. A sign that they always return to her), and escapes into the overworld.\n- Then he finds Shinki by chance, and decides she's his best chance of getting close to Jirou without getting caught (hiding behind possession)\n\t- At that point, her candle was small, but large enough to buy him time to get to Jirou\n- She wants money, and he has an idea. Give her shinigami eyes (omg like box jellyfish), and let her become a fake doctor. She'll go around, and eventually they'll find Jirou. Because he possesses her, she also has the power to drive away Shinigami (it's a Hiue thing).\n\t- When a shinigami is next to a jellyfish's bell, give up. Their fate is sealed, and the Grand Hiue will see to them. Messing with these will be bad idea\n\t- When a shinigami is at the end of their tentacles, death isn't in their fate and I'll lend you my power\n\t\t- The spell was something made up by Shinki to make it look more convincing. She could do it normally but that wouldn't make money. Quicktime events are meant to give player extra bonuses for looking the part.\n- Shinki helps the Nozakis. They don't pay as much, but they give her a talisman in case she wants to be rid of Shinigami kun\n\t- Shinigami kun is yapping with Saburou \n- When they're the most desperate for money- they suddenly get an offer from Jirou. Bingo. \n\t- Shinigami kun warns her not to heal him, no matter what. Shinki only gives him an empty promise. She needs money\n\t- They get there. Jirou got cancer in da balls and he's dying from it. Jirou's second wife promises Shinki a life-changing amount of money even just to heal him temporarily.\n\t- Shinki looks. Sees Shinigami kun at his feet. Jirou isn't actually promised to death, but Shinigami kun was planning to do something sneaky.\n\t\t- She sees he has a candle, but doesn't know why he's doing it.\n\t- Unfortunately it's bad for business if Jirou dies so Shinki has to thwart him somehow\n\t\t- She exorcises him, using a talisman from the Nozakis- using his own power against him.\n\t\t- When he starts slipping, though, he drags Shinki down to hell with him.\n- They both get taken to the cave of candles, which is actually more like a nice mansion. The Grand Hiue had renovations.\n\t- This is troubling because they're both about to be in big trouble if they're found by the Grand Hiue or any of her cronies.\n\t\t- He knows how to get out sneaky-like (back exits and stuff from his old janitorial gig) but Shinki is also very close to dying.\n\t- Shows Shinki her candle. The world around her goes dark, as the flame itself begins to wane. \n\t\t- He goes off on her for not trusting him. And for prioritizing money. \n\t- She wants to stay alive. Luckily, Shinigami kun has a solution\n\t- He takes out Jirou's candle- still burning brightly. He then dampens his fingers, and the candle goes out. \n\t\t- \"is that his candle?\"\n\t\t- \"Yes, but it'll flare  again unless you light it with your own flame. Well? What are you waiting for?\"\n\t- Shinigami kun watches, jeers, even. He wants her to survive, but only because he loathes seeing his brother live more.\n\t- Endings:\n\t\t- Failure: \n\t\t\t- The candle moves past a threshold before it's fully lit\n\t\t\t- Shinki dies, and Shinigami kun gets punished for his attempt on Jirou's life\n\t\t\t\t- This is probably canon\n\t\t- Success: \n\t\t\t- 1 percent chance shinki blows it out (rolled each time the scene happens for the speedrunners)\n\t\t\t\t- 0.5 percent chance shinki sneezes and blows it out (same as prev)\n\t\t\t\t- counts as the same ending as failure\n\t\t\t\t- \"Bad Luck Ending\"\n\t\t\t- Shinigami kun lets her escape, but when she gets home she falls asleep and gets jumped by another Shinigami for her transgressions.\n\t\t\t- ... Not for any particular reason. Just bad luck\n\t\t- Secret: \n\t\t\t- YanGami \n\t\t\t- (after taking her away, he decides that things would be better if their fates intertwined in life. Their lives were too poisoned up to this point. He sears a ring around her finger and his own, and vows to find her in reincarnation)\n\t\t\t\t- \"Love Ending\"\n\t\t\t\t- This ending threatens to take way too much of her agency tbh. It's not really a happy ending if she doesn't agree with it but goes along with it in the next life.\n\t\t\t\t- If we do go through this route, either: A - They're fated to overlap in every lifetime, but Shinigami will never have her or B - Shinki actually does fall for him somehow","x":1914,"y":-900,"width":1206,"height":1520},
		{"id":"d81597a19ecf0110","type":"text","text":"Maybe he switches their candles when Shinki gets deathly ill at some point- caused by being near Shinigami kun. Feels bad about this, but he's like \"I'll heal you\", goes into another room, and she gets miraculously better.\n\"What did you do?\"\n\"Shinigami stuff. Don't worry about it.\"\n(She'd ask too many questions, and he didn't want to admit he was just using her.)\n- Does he believe they share a bond that's more than just \"boss\" and \"employee\"?","x":1720,"y":-1180,"width":720,"height":220},
		{"id":"04488f0427eeb946","type":"text","text":"# Game Beats brainstorming\n---","x":-1776,"y":-2000,"width":393,"height":124,"color":"#ffa3f3"},
		{"id":"834988cee288485b","type":"text","text":"March 31 - Game Starts","x":-2760,"y":-1805,"width":250,"height":50,"color":"#feb171"},
		{"id":"5043fcafbeff1483","type":"text","text":"October 26 - Katsuo Strobilates","x":-2760,"y":-1938,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"#feb171"},
		{"id":"8cb82602e711067e","type":"text","text":"GAME TIMELINE","x":-2760,"y":-2050,"width":250,"height":50,"color":"#feb171"},
		{"id":"36ba8a876feb71b6","type":"text","text":"(I don't think I want the game to have more than 10 rounds, or it'll get boring)","x":-2440,"y":-2025,"width":250,"height":126},
		{"id":"7d6014e974691bea","type":"text","text":"### Endings (most result in you dying):\n--- \n* **Love ending**: Maybe kinda yandere? Not sure. \n\t* If you do a certain amount of events. Shinki becomes his raison d'ete, but after the betrayal he decides that he'll just keep her here. Forever.\n* **Candle endings**: Have the candle scene. Hold the candle with the mouse and wait until its lit fully. \n\t* If the player moves the candle before it's //fully// lit, she will die. Shinigami kun will talk while this happens so if the player moves mouse to move along with his dialogue, they die (\"Haha. You think you could light anything with those shakey hands?\", \"It's going oooout, see seee seeeeeeee?\"). You just have to hold still and let him talk. (God. This is peak role embodiment tho, You have to ignore him)\n\t\t* Note: Maybe have the candle shake a little by itself and you have to fangangle against it? I like that better lowk\n\t\t* The shinigami will still talk but if you don't fanangle against Shinki's hands while you read then you die\n    * If player lights the candle\n    \t* 1% chance she sneezes and blows it out (get fucked lol) (rolls each time the scene is loaded for the completionists)\n        * Otherwise, Shinigami kun just claps and disappears- ending the interaction and friendship coldly.\n        * Then Shinki goes home as if nothing ever happend...\n        \t* Actually, when Shinki goes to sleep, she sees him by the head of her futon. \"Shit\"\n            * If you didn't buy ofuda (very hard, you need to make a lot of money and fight Shinki on the menuing), the game ends there. Otherwise, you slap the ofuda on him and uh, it gives you enough time to escape. \n            * The win is empty though, and you're back to square one. Now with a shinigami on your heels. Escape the country and change your name. ","x":-4540,"y":-660,"width":1120,"height":700},
		{"id":"66a0c6d686d31bbc","type":"text","text":"- Endings:\n\t- Let Go:\n\t\t- Pay the Nozakis to exorcise Shinigami\n\t\t- \"I'm not sure why I did this. I guess I'm back at square one\"\n\t\t- She dies shortly after.\n\t- Failure: \n\t\t- The candle moves past a threshold before it's fully lit\n\t\t- Shinki dies, and Shinigami kun gets punished for his attempt on Jirou's life\n\t\t\t- This is probably canon\n\t- Success: \n\t\t- 1 percent chance shinki blows it out (rolled each time the scene happens for the speedrunners)\n\t\t\t- 0.5 percent chance shinki sneezes and blows it out (same as prev)\n\t\t\t- counts as the same ending as failure\n\t\t\t- \"Bad Luck Ending\"\n\t\t- Shinigami kun lets her escape\n\t\t\t- He eats her old candle so they don't find about what happened. Why? Because even though she betrayed him, he can't help but save her. \n\t\t- When she gets home, she falls asleep and gets jumped by another Shinigami \n\t\t\t- ... Not for any particular reason. Just bad luck\n\t- Secret: \n\t\t- YanGami \n\t\t- (after taking her away, he decides that things would be better if their fates intertwined in life. Their lives were too poisoned up to this point. He sears a ring around her finger and his own, and vows to find her in reincarnation)\n\t\t\t- \"Love Ending\"\n\t\t\t- This ending threatens to take way too much of her agency tbh. It's not really a happy ending if she doesn't agree with it but goes along with it in the next life.\n\t\t\t- If we do go through this route, either: A - They're fated to overlap in every lifetime, but Shinigami will never have her or B - Shinki actually does fall for him somehow","x":-3420,"y":-740,"width":920,"height":1440},
		{"id":"0bc5b0c2c653458d","type":"text","text":"April - First 4 rounds","x":-2760,"y":-1720,"width":250,"height":50,"color":"#feb171"},
